From e26151b5f5ef179c288a11cc04a75360f7195710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreeyash Pandey <shrpand@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 03:41:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Use 4 byte alignment for except_ordered section
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

picolibc.ld.in uses ALIGN(8) inside .except_unordered before
PROVIDE(__exidx_start = .). When the prior section ends 4-byte (not
8-byte) aligned, ALIGN(8) bumps the symbol +4, but ELD emits the
ARM_EXIDX content at the section base. So __exidx_start lands 4 bytes
(half an entry) into the table; libunwind decodes every entry off-by-4,
the binary search in getInfoFromEHABISection() misses, and unwinding
stops at frame 1. Breaks libunwind_01, libunwind_02, and
backtrace/forced-unwind on all ARM EHABI variants.

Per IHI0038 §6 [1] an index entry is two 4-byte words, so the table only
needs word (4-byte) alignment.

[1] https://github.com/ARM-software/abi-aa/blob/main/legacy-documents/ehabi32/ihi0038_B/IHI0038B_ehabi.pdf

Signed-off-by: Shreeyash Pandey <shrpand@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 picolibc.ld.in | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/picolibc.ld.in b/picolibc.ld.in
index 59f6e9566..1f8d9d9f4 100644
--- a/picolibc.ld.in
+++ b/picolibc.ld.in
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@ SECTIONS
 	} >flash AT>flash :text
 
 	.except_unordered : {
-		. = ALIGN(@DEFAULT_ALIGNMENT@);
+		. = ALIGN(4);
 
 		PROVIDE(@PREFIX@__exidx_start = .);
 		*(.ARM.exidx*)
-- 
2.34.1

